# issue #80 (nested existential monotonicity), the three-axiom minimal case:
# C ⊑ ∃t.∃u.A, A ⊑ F, ∃t.∃u.F ⊑ D entails C ⊑ D by plain monotonicity. Konclude
# reports both (A,F) and (C,D); rustdl reports only (A,F). flat-mono.ofn is the
# NON-nested sibling rustdl gets right — nesting alone is the trigger.
provenance: konclude-v0.7.0-1138
subclass: C D
